{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Change pushed: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2664\n\nCommit `44a916fdb97b`. NOT submitted and this ticket is NOT closed — the operator\nverifies the votes and submits.\n\n### Seeded-defect evidence (the test has teeth)\n\nNew oracles applied to **unmodified `origin/main` source** (`268bc9733`):\n\n```\n7 failed, 65 passed\n  ...[output-never-set-refuses]      assert 0 == 1\n  ...[empty-output-refuses]          assert 0 == 1\n  ...[unrecognised-casing-refuses]   assert 0 == 1\n  ...[unrecognised-value-refuses]    assert 0 == 1\n  test_a_missing_verdict_writes_nothing_at_all[unset]   assert 0 == 1\n  test_a_missing_verdict_writes_nothing_at_all[empty]   assert 0 == 1\n  test_a_crashed_audit_is_distinguishable...  assert (0, 0) == (1, 0)\ncaptured stdout: \"Closed advisory ticket abcd-0000-1111-2222 — advisories cleared.\"\n```\n\nAll 65 pre-existing tests passed unchanged, so the new ones fail ONLY on the defect.\nWith the fix: **72 passed**. Seeding the one-line defect back (restoring\n`environ.get(\"BLOCKING\", \"false\") == \"true\"` and dropping the guard): **7 failed, 65\npassed** again. Restoring: **72 passed**.\n\nOriginal reproduction, re-run against the fixed code — the table inverts exactly where\nit should and nowhere else:\n\n```\naudit CRASHED (BLOCKING never set)  rc=1  FORCE-CLOSE=no\naudit CRASHED (BLOCKING='')         rc=1  FORCE-CLOSE=no\nadvisories genuinely cleared        rc=0  FORCE-CLOSE=YES\nadvisory STILL blocking             rc=0  FORCE-CLOSE=no\ncrash-argv == genuine-clear-argv ?  False       (was True)\n```\n\n### Suites run, and NOT run\n\nThe host was at load average 32-45 (18 cores, ~11 active worktrees, two full `make\nverify` runs already in flight), so per the coordinator's scheduling instruction a third\nfull suite was NOT started. Stated explicitly so the gap is visible rather than assumed:\n\n- RAN: `tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py` (72), the affected-module set\n  (`test_alert_dedup`, `test_canary_bridge`, `test_canary_bridge_heldout`,\n  `test_dependency_advisory_wiring`, `test_transition_force_flag_24f7`) — 180 passed;\n  the whole-tree AST-scan family, all 37 modules importing `_tree_scan`/\n  `parsed_python_files` — 593 passed, 3 skipped.\n- RAN: `make lint` (exit 0), `make typecheck` (763 files clean), complexity ratchet\n  (`new=0 increased=0`), mechanism ratchet (`new=0 increased=0`).\n- NOT RUN: full `make verify` / the whole `tests/` tree. Left to CI's `Verified` gate.\n\nAll runs used the BARE `pytest` console script from the worktree venv, not\n`python -m pytest`.\n\n### Risk to other sessions\n\nNone identified. The change adds no repo-wide check — the new tests are scoped to\n`cmd_advisory_alert`, and the workflow edit is a comment. Nothing here can fire against\nhealthy `main` for an unrelated reason."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788589233564948001,"uuid":"2b436e70-f9be-4adb-a32e-277c3c88d73f"}